NAME
       stty - show or change the settings of the terminal

SYNOPSIS
       stty [-a]
       stty SETTING...

DESCRIPTION
       stty shows or changes how the terminal treats what you type: which key
       erases a character, which key interrupts a program (Ctrl+C), whether
       typed characters are echoed, and the size of the window. Scripts use
       "stty -echo" to hide what is typed (a password) and "stty echo" to
       turn echoing back on.

       If a program left the terminal in a strange state (nothing you type
       shows up), typing "stty sane" and pressing Enter usually fixes it.

OPTIONS
       -a     Print all current settings.

       echo, -echo
              Show, or hide, the characters you type.

       sane   Reset the settings to reasonable values.

EXAMPLES
           stty -echo; read -r secret; stty echo

SEE ALSO
       tty(1), tput(1), reset(1)
